{"nodes": [{"id": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_issues_03_pr_15_plus_bp_model_run_pr_15_plus_bp_model_run", "label": "Issue 03: PR 15+ BP Model Run", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/issues/03-pr-15-plus-bp-model-run.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolved. Because the external primary-model-pipeline spec was not implemented, it was built first as the shared seam (pipeline.py with TrainingConfig/TrainingResult/run_training_pipeline, modeling.py, calibration.py, metrics.py, feature_policy.py, model_bundle.py) so the PR run reuses it instead of growing a second path. PR-specific work is configuration only in src/screener/pr_model.py: pr_15_plus_config sets the PR table, age >= 15, BP-valid filters, target, cluster grouping, household, weight_scaled, and PR subgroups, with the 12-feature default. scripts/run_pr_model.py adds --sample, --smoke, --bootstrap, --shap-sample, --no-split-assignment, --feature-variant; smoke samples after filtering so it never trains on the full table. A review pass fixed weighted prevalence, cluster-label alignment in the bootstrap, the ignored split_assignment_path, and missing report sections."}], "edges": [{"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_issues_03_pr_15_plus_bp_model_run_pr_15_plus_bp_model_run", "target": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_spec_pr_15_plus_bp_sensitivity_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".scratch/pr-bp-sensitivity-model/issues/03-pr-15-plus-bp-model-run.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_issues_03_pr_15_plus_bp_model_run_pr_15_plus_bp_model_run", "target": "_scratch_pr_bp_sensitivity_model_issues_02_pr_split_reuse_and_assignment_pr_split_reuse_and_assignment", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".sc